00:43:03.020 --> 00:43:11.080
President Bongbong Marcos (video): Kaya pinagtutuunan natin na mabuti ang ating mga tren, mga busway, transport hub at integrated terminal

asr-001124
00:43:11.080 --> 00:43:16.360
President Bongbong Marcos (video): at ang pagpapaganda at pagpapalawak ng mga paliparan at pantalan sa buong bansa.

asr-001125
00:43:16.360 --> 00:43:29.800
President Bongbong Marcos (video): Ito ay upang mas malawak at malayo ang naaabot, tumaas ang kapasidad at maging moderno at mas maginhawa ang serbisyo.

asr-001125-split-2
00:43:29.800 --> 00:43:46.360
Presentation video: The Department of Transportation has been relentless in achieving significant strides to improve the country's public transport system. President Ferdinand Marcos Jr. has ordered the DOTr to expedite the construction of critical big-ticket transport infrastructure projects and initiate commuter-focused

asr-001126
00:43:46.360 --> 00:44:16.340
Presentation video: programs to ease the daily commute of Filipinos. Among the commuter-centric initiatives the DOTr has implemented were the 50% discounts for senior citizens, students and persons with disabilities, the One P3 Familia Pass promo and 12 days of Christmas Libreng Sakay across major lines to encourage commuters and motorists to use public transport and at the same time help them save on transport costs. The government also relaunched the iconic Love Bus

asr-001127
00:44:16.360 --> 00:44:46.340
Presentation video: Libreng Sakay initiative through the service contracting program, providing free and reliable public transportation in major urban areas including Metro Manila, Metro Cebu and Metro Davao. Personalized white beep cards with an automatic 50% discount were distributed to senior citizens, PWDs and students riding MRT-3, LRT-1 and LRT-2. The DOTr continues to improve MRT-3 facilities, ensuring passenger

asr-001128
00:44:46.360 --> 00:44:59.980
Presentation video: comfort and safety while eliminating long queues and speeding up commuter entry at stations. Tension in the Middle East early this year made a heavy impact in many countries, including the Philippines. Under Uplift, the DOTr and its attached agencies

asr-001129
00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:13.940
Presentation video: implemented recalibrated support packages that include fare discounts, free rides, fuel subsidy, terminal fee discount, toll discount, rebates on transport charges, and the service contracting program, among others.

asr-001130
00:45:14.360 --> 00:45:18.580
Presentation video: All this to cushion the impact of the Middle East crisis on commuters and motorists.

asr-001131
00:45:18.580 --> 00:45:31.580
Presentation video: As part of the Uplift initiatives, President Marcos Jr. led the launch of the service contracting program at Araneta Center Bus Terminal in Quezon City and the fuel subsidy program at Parañaque Integrated Terminal Exchange.

asr-001132
00:45:32.320 --> 00:45:38.720
Presentation video: The DOTR likewise continues to implement a 50% fare discount to all passengers with MRT-3 and LRT-2.

asr-001133
00:45:41.220 --> 00:45:47.360
Presentation video: In the railway sector, the DOTr is speeding up the construction of mass transit railway systems.

asr-001134
00:45:47.360 --> 00:45:48.560
Presentation video: One of the biggest is

asr-001135
00:45:48.560 --> 00:45:54.380
Presentation video: the Metro Manila Subway Project, which is fast taking shape underground from Valenzuela to NAIA.

asr-001136
00:45:55.220 --> 00:46:10.920
Presentation video: Once operational, the 33-kilometer 17-station Metro Manila Subway Project, which will run from Valenzuela City to Naia, will reduce travel time from 90 minutes to just 41 minutes, and will benefit around 519,000 passengers daily.

asr-001137
00:46:11.680 --> 00:46:17.960
Presentation video: On the other hand, the North-South Commuter Railways Valenzuela to Malolo segment will be operational next year.

asr-001138
00:46:18.560 --> 00:46:31.420
Presentation video: Once fully operational, the 147-kilometer rail line can service 800,000 passengers daily, reducing travel time between Clark-Pampanga and Calamba-Laguna from over 4 hours to just 2 hours.

asr-001139
00:46:31.680 --> 00:46:40.140
Presentation video: Preparations for the NSCR's operations and maintenance are underway, through the public-private partnership market-sounding activities being held in different countries.

asr-001140
00:46:40.400 --> 00:46:47.840
Presentation video: Relocation activities are also ongoing and progressing in Cavite, Laguna, and Pampanga to support communities affected by the said project.

asr-001141
00:46:48.560 --> 00:46:59.000
Presentation video: Meanwhile, the MRT-7's first 12 stations are expected to be operational by second quarter of next year, connecting North Avenue in Quezon City to Sacred Heart in Caloocan.

asr-001142
00:46:59.720 --> 00:47:11.200
Presentation video: Once the project is completed, connecting Quezon City all the way to Bulacan will cut travel time from 2 to 3 hours to just 35 minutes, and can serve up to 850,000 passengers daily.

asr-001143
00:47:11.840 --> 00:47:17.880
Presentation video: Existing rail infrastructure is also being rehabilitated to provide an improved and more convenient travel experience for commuters.

asr-001144
00:47:18.560 --> 00:47:37.260
Presentation video: The rehabilitation of MRT-3's Quezon Avenue station offers clearer and larger wayfinding signs, cleaner and more accessible restrooms, wider passenger spaces, improved ventilation, and platform window louvers and tactile tiles for persons with visual impairment.

asr-001145
00:47:37.260 --> 00:47:48.260
Presentation video: These upgrades are designed to make commuting easier, and as Quezon Avenue station sets the pace for improvements, other MRT-3 stations are set to follow suit as rehabilitation works continue.

asr-001146
00:47:48.560 --> 00:47:56.600
Presentation video: At the center of Metro Manila's growing rail network is the Common Station, or the Unified Grand Central Station.

asr-001147
00:47:57.440 --> 00:48:05.800
Presentation video: By connecting LRT-1, MRT-3, and MRT-7, it will ensure seamless transfers for at least 1.28 million passengers.

asr-001148
